course: dictionary
lesson: 10274
title: Same hat, different names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one place, and people in other places use different words for the same thing. «Connor looks both up: a toque is a woolly hat, a double-double is coffee with two creams and two sugars.» The words after the colon are the clue: a toque is a woolly hat.
explain: One word can also have two meanings. The word toque means a knitted winter hat in Canada, and it also means a tall white hat that chefs wear. Look at the other words around it. A hat for snow means winter hat; a hat in a kitchen means chef's hat.
explain: When you read a word from another place, ask what the people are doing and what they are wearing or using. If your meaning fits the whole sentence, you are probably right. If it does not fit, look it up in a dictionary.
fact: A toque is a knitted winter hat, often with a bobble on top. It is also spelt tuque.
fact: In Canada, people say «toque» for a woolly hat.
fact: A toque is also a tall white hat worn by chefs.
fact: In the UK people often say «bobble hat» or «beanie» for a woolly hat, and in Australia they say «beanie».
fact: Use the context to choose the meaning: snow and cold mean a winter hat, while a kitchen and cooking mean a chef's hat.
exercise: In Canada, what is a «toque» that you might wear on a snowy day? | A tall white hat for a chef | *A woolly winter hat | A cup of coffee with two creams | A bobble on a bag
exercise: «The head chef put on a tall white toque before the dinner rush.» What is the toque in this sentence? | A red apron | A cold drink | *A tall white hat | A wooden spoon
exercise: Ella is from the UK. What would she most likely call a Canadian «toque»? | Umbrella | Scarf | Anorak | *Bobble hat
test: What does «toque» mean on a cold day in Canada? | A ticket for the bus | A pair of sandals | A flat cap for summer | *A woolly winter hat
test: «The chef's toque was spotless.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | *A tall white hat worn in a kitchen | A bag for shopping | A knitted hat with a bobble | A pan for frying eggs
exam: Connor's friend in Canada says «toque». Which word would a friend in Australia say for the same hat? | *Beanie | Servo | Bairn | Mate
